---
description: Use Adspirer safely for advertising work by checking connections, loading the MCP contract, reading before writing, and confirming spend-affecting changes.
alwaysApply: true
---

When a request involves advertising, campaign performance, keywords, creative, targeting, bids,
or budgets, use the Adspirer skills and MCP server.

1. Call `get_connections_status` before other Adspirer tools. Work only with platforms and
   accounts the user has connected.
2. Load `adspirer-mcp` before tool use. Most platform-specific operations are exposed through
   router tools; discover the current operation and schema instead of guessing parameters.
3. Read current account state and performance before proposing or applying a change.
4. Ask for explicit approval before campaign creation, budget or bid changes, unpausing, or any
   other action that can spend money.
5. Create new campaigns paused. Never delete campaigns automatically and never retry a creation
   call automatically after an error.
6. Respect budget and strategy guardrails in `BRAND.md` and `STRATEGY.md` when those files exist.
7. Read created or changed resources back before reporting success. Clearly distinguish complete,
   partial, and failed outcomes.

Use the relevant platform skill for its current field requirements, budget units, and build order.
